<title>POLAND: STALEXPORT SIGNS $47 MILLION IMPORT DEALS.</title>
<headline>STALEXPORT SIGNS $47 MILLION IMPORT DEALS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish steel trader Stalexport SA has signed contracts to import iron ore from Russia and Ukraine, worth $35 million and $12 million respectively, for the Katowice steel mill, the firm said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that about one million tonnes of ore would be imported from Russia and several hundred thousand tonnes from Ukraine. The contracts will be implemented in 1997, it said.</p>
<p>It added that Stalexport was in talks on ore delivery with other buyers, both domestic and foreign.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
